Third-party data

The validation targets under testdata/validation/targets/ include data and values from the
works below, each under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International licence,
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/. testdata/validation/targets/LICENCES.toml is the
full ledger, with the terms of every source the targets cite.

Data from J. Biber, T. Jones, A. Champneys, R. Green and R. Szalai, "Measurements and linearized models for golf ball bounce on a green", Sports Engineering (2023), https://doi.org/10.1007/s12283-023-00442-4, Online Resource 2, licensed under CC BY 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/).
Changes: The two CSV files are unmodified. bib.json restates their rows in m/s and rad/s (columns times the ball radius 0.021335 m for velocity) and adds the earlier implementation's predictions.
Files: bib.json, biber-2023/data_campaignA.csv, biber-2023/data_campaignB.csv.

Lift fit from Lyu, Kensrud, Smith and Tosaya, "Aerodynamics of golf balls in still air", Proceedings 2(6) 238 (2018), https://doi.org/10.3390/proceedings2060238, CC BY 4.0.
Changes: Values computed from the published fit Cl = -3.25 S^2 + 1.99 S at three spin ratios.
Files: lyu18.json.

Lift coefficients from Li, Tsubokura and Tsunoda, Flow Turbulence Combust 99(3) 837-864 (2017), https://doi.org/10.1007/s10494-017-9859-1, CC BY 4.0.
Changes: Three values taken from the text.
Files: li17.json.

Face-angle shares from Wood, Henrikson and Broadie, Proceedings 2(6) 249 (2018), https://doi.org/10.3390/proceedings2060249, CC BY 4.0.
Changes: Three means and confidence intervals taken from the text.
Files: ping.json.

Cup outcomes from Hogan and Antali, "Mechanics of the golf lip out", R. Soc. Open Sci. 12(11) 250907 (2025), https://doi.org/10.1098/rsos.250907, CC BY 4.0. The centre capture speed is Holmes (1991) as quoted there.
Changes: Values read from figures 5 and 7 and the text.
Files: c1.json, c2.json.

